{
  "credit": "Mjolnir 3D model (same geometry as mjolnir_thrown.json), generated from the Blockbench export \"minecraftmodels/model.json\" -- geometry uniformly scaled and translated so its bounding box is byte-for-byte the one the previous model occupied (x centred on 8, z centred on 8, y 0.5..14.375). That is deliberate and load-bearing: every display transform below, and MjolnirEntityRenderer.UPRIGHT_LIFT (which is derived from the model top sitting 6.375px above centre), are tuned to those exact bounds, so re-fitting the new geometry into them is what lets a completely different mesh drop in without re-deriving a single pose. Every element then carries an identical Z-axis rotation baked in via the standard per-element rotation field (origin [8,8,8], -45 degrees) -- this is what Minecraft itself uses to pre-rotate box geometry before baking, confirmed from FaceBakery.applyElementRotation bytecode (Quaternionf.rotationAxis, standard right-hand rule, verified against this project's own Rz(theta) convention). That rotation carries the model's local +Y handle-to-head axis onto the same diagonal a vanilla tool sprite's icon is drawn along. The display block below is copied VERBATIM from minecraft:item/handheld_mace (hand contexts) and minecraft:item/generated (ground/head/fixed) -- zero custom rotation, translation or scale numbers of our own anywhere in this file. Do not replace this with hand-tuned rotation/translation/scale values without an actual in-game screenshot to check against.",
